{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-leading-term-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:leading-term-data","kind":"definition","title":"Leading monomial, coefficient, and term","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-monomial-basis"],"cites":["references/leitnerpawloski2004"],"tags":["groebner-basis","leading-term"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.LeadingTerm","text":"leading-term-data.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/leading-term-data.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:leading-term-data\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> be a <a href=\"#def:monomial-basis\">monomial basis</a> well-ordered by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code>.\nFor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\in A</code>, write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> uniquely as</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  f = c_1 b_1 + c_2 b_2 + \\cdots + c_n b_n,\n  \\qquad c_i \\in R^* := R \\setminus \\{0\\},\\;\n  b_i \\in B,\\;\n  b_1 > b_2 > \\cdots > b_n.</code></pre>\n<p>Then define:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the <strong>leading monomial</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LM}(f) := b_1</code>,</li>\n<li>the <strong>leading coefficient</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LC}(f) := c_1</code>,</li>\n<li>the <strong>leading term</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LT}(f) := \\mathrm{LC}(f)\\,\\mathrm{LM}(f)</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/leading-term-data.md","heading":"Definition","number":"2.2.2"}
